{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1221017-would-like-a-source-for-a-koldunic-related-matter","id":1221017,"title":"Would Like a Source for a Koldunic Related Matter","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-21T18:28:43-07:00","id":1221017,"title":"Would Like a Source for a Koldunic Related Matter","content":"Hello all. i've got a question for the scholars out there. I was looking at the White Wolf Wikia,and in the Koldunic Sorcery pagethere is the following quote<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The older form of Koldunic Sorcery practiced specific </span></span></span><i>krainas</i><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> instead of Paths. While Paths are standardized, each kraina is unique to the domain the </span></span></span><i>koldun</i><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> claims as his own and it often takes decades for the aspiring </span></span></span><i>koldun</i><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> before he has a bond with his domain close enough to properly use his primary kraina. During </span></span></span><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Kupala%27s_Eve?redlink=1&amp;action=edit&amp;flow=create-page-article-redlink\" target=\"_blank\">Kupala's Eve</a><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, some Tzimisce abandoned this form as weak and inefficient and instead turned to </span></span></span><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Kupala\" target=\"_blank\">Kupala</a><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, who twisted the </span></span></span><i>krainas</i><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> into the elemental paths used in the </span></span></span><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Modern_Nights\" target=\"_blank\">Modern Nights</a><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">. Only a handful of Tzimisce Elders still practices the old form, most of them in allegiance with the </span></span></span><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Tal%27Mahe%27Ra\" target=\"_blank\">Tal'Mahe'Ra</a><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">. Some have begun to instruct members of the </span></span></span><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Order_of_Moloch\" target=\"_blank\">Order of Moloch</a><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> into the old art.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Can anyone tell me the source of this information?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T18:53:57-07:00","id":1221029,"title":"","content":"Try the following<ul><li><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/DAV\" target=\"_blank\">DAV</a>: <b><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Players_Guide_to_High_Clans\" target=\"_blank\">Players Guide to High Clans</a></b>, p. 182-189</li> <li><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/VTM\" target=\"_blank\">VTM</a>: <b><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Clanbook:_Tzimisce_Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Clanbook: Tzimisce Revised</a></b>, p. 64</li> <li><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/VTM\" target=\"_blank\">VTM</a>: <b><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Blood_Magic:_Secrets_of_Thaumaturgy\" target=\"_blank\">Blood Magic: Secrets of Thaumaturgy</a></b>, p. 131-132</li> <li><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/V20\" target=\"_blank\">V20</a>: <b><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Rites_of_the_Blood\" target=\"_blank\">Rites of the Blood</a></b>, p. 156-158</li> <li><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/V20\" target=\"_blank\">V20</a>: <b><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Vampire:_The_Dark_Ages_20th_Anniversary_Edition\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Dark Ages 20th Anniversary Edition</a></b>, p. 274-278</li> <li><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/V20\" target=\"_blank\">V20</a>: <b><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/The_Black_Hand:_A_Guide_to_the_Tal%27Mahe%27Ra\" target=\"_blank\">The Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra</a></b>, p. 169-174</li> <li><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/V20\" target=\"_blank\">V20</a>: <b><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Tome_of_Secrets\" target=\"_blank\">Tome of Secrets</a></b>, p. 44-48</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T18:54:03-07:00","id":1221030,"title":"","content":"I also would like to know which book first describes Koldunic Sorcery if you don't mind","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T19:04:07-07:00","id":1221033,"title":"","content":"Hey.<br /> <br /> First try the links at the bottom of the page for the references<br /> <br /> DAV: Players Guide to High Clans, p. 182-189<br /> VTM: Clanbook: Tzimisce Revised, p. 64<br /> VTM: Blood Magic: Secrets of Thaumaturgy, p. 131-132<br /> V20: Rites of the Blood, p. 156-158<br /> V20: Vampire: The Dark Ages 20th Anniversary Edition, p. 274-278<br /> V20: The Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra, p. 169-174<br /> V20: Tome of Secrets, p. 44-48<br /> <br /> The links for the books describe what's in them, and when released<br /> <br /> DAV: Players Guide to High Clans, 2003<br /> VTM: Clanbook: Tzimisce Revised, 2001<br /> VTM: Blood Magic: Secrets of Thaumaturgy, 2000<br /> V20: Rites of the Blood, 2014<br /> V20: Vampire: The Dark Ages 20th Anniversary Edition, 2015<br /> V20: The Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra, 2016<br /> V20: Tome of Secrets, 2016<br /> <br /> So we can see that VTM Blood Magic: Secrets of Thaumaturgy was the first in 2000.<br /> <br /> Kraina came about in V20. And is a much better way for the powers to operate","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T19:54:14-07:00","id":1221044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1221017-would-like-a-source-for-a-koldunic-related-matter?p=1221033#post1221033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kraina came about in V20. And is a much better way for the powers to operate</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't dispute that the Kraina system came about in V20, but I do think it's opinion that they're necessarily better. I, for one, find them interesting, but not better. Not worse, either, mind you. Just a different way of doing things. And, personally, I'd run Kraina and Ways all in one Koldunic Sorcery package.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;At the risk of sounding like a murder hobo&quot;<br /> <br /> Attributed to Nyrufa.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24134-inertial-frame","name":"Inertial Frame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T20:48:39-07:00","id":1221060,"title":"","content":"Of course it is just an opinion. There'e no objective way to decide.<br /> <br /> My Main ST uses Kraina for dark ages, old Tzimesce with pacts in the homeland; and Ways for modern and the Sabbat as a method without ties to the spirits of the land in Transylvania. Old Tzimesce will still have Kraina, and may have both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T07:44:48-07:00","id":1221152,"title":"","content":"Thank you both","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T14:48:25-07:00","id":1221263,"title":"","content":"Outside way of sorrow I think the ways are objectively worse, they don't particularly play up aspects of slavic magic/folklore and add to things that have no real baring in it..(I'm looking at you way of fire 5) there's no reason for why ways exist vs refluffing other blood magic(say Lure of flames to way of flames etc) except.. its supposed to better cover the themes of koldun but.. they don't at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T05:39:58-07:00","id":1221457,"title":"","content":"Actually Dark Age 20 is where Kraina Comes from, and the Talmaherah book is what bridges the gap saying Kraina is the old ways, and the new Ways of the 5 elemental Paths are a result of Kupala offering a corrupted form of Koldunic sorcery based off of his Elemental corruption of the Genius Loci being taught in exchange for foresaking the Kraina.<br /> <br /> I like Kraina bit more because of the flavor, and well something is off when everyone can summon volcanoes...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T15:32:54-07:00","id":1221858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1221017-would-like-a-source-for-a-koldunic-related-matter?p=1221457#post1221457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like Kraina bit more because of the flavor, and well something is off when everyone can summon volcanoes...</div> </div> </div> </div>Its more the idea that Koldun is Slavic magic when there doesn't appear to be a volcano in the time slavs have been in Eastern europe. Now if someone wanted to have Magic from Iceland or Hawaii or even Italy that called upon Volcanos..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T16:54:20-07:00","id":1221880,"title":"","content":"I don't think you can back date logic. The ways were based on elements in general in the previous edition and not Slavic magic; and then the writer/s for DAV20 thought of a more locally thematic folklore based magic system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T21:56:53-07:00","id":1221944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1221017-would-like-a-source-for-a-koldunic-related-matter?p=1221880#post1221880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you can back date logic. The ways were based on elements in general in the previous edition and not Slavic magic; and then the writer/s for DAV20 thought of a more locally thematic folklore based magic system.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You have way of Sorrow that at least tries to play at being based on slavic and you have way of Fire that plays at being generic but then it has volcano powers which requires a fairly high degree of scientific knowledge AND is redundant because &quot;Generic Fire magic path&quot; already exists in Lure of Flames(As does &quot;Generic water&quot; and &quot;Generic storm&quot;). Either go wholesale in Kraina or go wholesale and make it a similar blood magic like everyone else.. I mean Duranki is far more focused on Spirit it doesn't get &quot;Keys of Solomon that do everything in spirit manipu but so much better&quot; and Akhu doesn't have &quot;Like Weather control but so much better because SET&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T09:37:21-07:00","id":1223297,"title":"","content":"The quoted passage in the original post is from <i>V20: The Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra</i>.<br /> <br /> I've come around to liking the individualized system of Krainas for the old-school practice of Tzimisce magic, but I still think the ones written out in the DAV material are a hodgepodge of powers that don't look like they belong together. The new Krainas in the Black Hand book at least have thematic unity (while not appealing to me personally, but that's a matter of individual taste rather than objecting to how they're designed).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}